%% The TuiClose model as a chart, for today's code. Each red state breaks the rule named.
%% Events the chart leaves out: the request ending by itself, an alternate-screen close,
%% the closer thread failing to start (the in-handler fallback), and loop blocking (design b).
stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    [*] --> Starting: you start fx
    Starting --> RawNoHandler: raw mode is on, handlers not yet installed
    Starting --> Ready: handlers installed after raw mode
    RawNoHandler --> Ready: handlers installed
    RawNoHandler --> EndedRawTty: a signal arrives (BREAKS TtyRestored)
    Ready --> Turn: you send a message
    Turn --> Ready: the reply ends
    Ready --> FullScreen: you open the transcript
    FullScreen --> Ready: you close it
    Ready --> Shutting: you quit with /exit
    Turn --> Shutting: you quit with /exit (cancels the request)
    Shutting --> Ended: releaseTerminal restores the tty
    Shutting --> EndedRawTty: TERM/HUP after uninstall before disableRawMode (BREAKS TtyRestored)
    Shutting --> Shutting: SIGINT is ignored by the guard
    Ready --> Closing: SIGTERM or SIGHUP
    Turn --> Closing: SIGTERM or SIGHUP
    FullScreen --> Closing: SIGTERM or SIGHUP
    Closing --> EndedRawTty: screen restored, tty left raw (BREAKS TtyRestored)
    Ready --> EndedRawTty: SIGINT, no handler (BREAKS TtyRestored)
    FullScreen --> EndedRawTty: SIGINT, screen left open (BREAKS TtyRestored)
    Turn --> EndedUnsaved: SIGINT during a turn (BREAKS CloseSavesRequest)
    Turn --> EndedSaved: SIGTERM during a turn, request saved clean
    EndedRawTty --> [*]
    EndedUnsaved --> [*]
    EndedSaved --> [*]
    Ended --> [*]
